       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum for acute pain or inflammatory conditions.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is the usual dose for pain or fever.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
